.TH HYPRMONCFG 1 "@MAN_DATE@" "hyprmoncfg @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyprmoncfg \- manage monitor layouts and profiles for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprmoncfg
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprmoncfg
is an interactive terminal layout editor and command-line profile manager for
Hyprland. It can arrange monitors, save hardware-aware profiles, apply them
safely, and manage workspace assignments.
.PP
Running the program without a command launches the interactive terminal UI.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Launch the interactive terminal UI.
.TP
.B monitors
List monitors reported by Hyprland.
.TP
.B profiles
List saved monitor profiles.
.TP
.BI "save " name
Save the current monitor state as a profile.
.TP
.BI "apply " name
Apply a saved profile.
.TP
.BI "delete " name
Delete a saved profile.
.TP
.B doctor
Check that Hyprland reads the generated monitor configuration last.
.TP
.B manage
Let hyprmoncfg manage the active monitor configuration.
.TP
.B status
Show the current profile and daemon status.
.TP
.B unmanage
Hand monitor configuration back to Hyprland.
.TP
.B version
Show build version information.
.TP
.B completion
Generate shell completion code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config-dir " directory
Use an alternative profile configuration directory.
.TP
.BI "--monitors-conf " file
Write the generated monitor configuration to an alternative path.
.TP
.BI "--hypr-config " file
Use an alternative Hyprland root configuration for include verification.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Show the program version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprmoncfg/profiles/
Saved profiles and their generated Hyprland sidecars.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/monitors.conf
Default generated monitor configuration for legacy Hyprland configurations.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua
Default generated monitor configuration when Hyprland Lua configuration is
active.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hyprmoncfgd (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
.PP
Full documentation is available at https://hyprmoncfg.dev.
